428
00:15:54,858 --> 00:15:56,125
- I'll soon see him.

429
00:15:56,125 --> 00:15:56,958
- [Crow] In hell.

430
00:15:56,958 --> 00:15:58,055
- It'll be wonderful.

431
00:15:58,055 --> 00:15:59,646
- How long since you've
seen your brother, Vena?

432
00:15:59,646 --> 00:16:00,479
- [Joel] An hour.

433
00:16:00,479 --> 00:16:01,924
- Almost three years.

434
00:16:01,924 --> 00:16:06,091
He'll be on the Casa 7
project another five years.

435
00:16:07,594 --> 00:16:08,541
What happened, Reggie?

436
00:16:08,541 --> 00:16:11,109
- [Tom] Ah, the Playboy
channel's scrambled again.

437
00:16:11,109 --> 00:16:13,086
- All the instruments are dead.

438
00:16:13,086 --> 00:16:13,919
- [Joel] So am I.

439
00:16:13,919 --> 00:16:14,971
- Well it seems normal.

440
00:16:14,971 --> 00:16:16,612
- This is weird.

441
00:16:16,612 --> 00:16:17,945
- [Tom] So am I.

442
00:16:20,475 --> 00:16:21,801
- Rocket thrust is zero.

443
00:16:21,801 --> 00:16:24,294
- [Crow] Gee that makes me bitter.

444
00:16:24,294 --> 00:16:26,182
- [Tom] Oh, and the animation sucks too.

445
00:16:26,182 --> 00:16:28,202
- [Crow] Oh brother.

446
00:16:28,202 --> 00:16:31,671
- [Joel] M-C-7, are they
any relation to the MC5?

447
00:16:31,671 --> 00:16:32,836
- [Tom] Maybe.

448
00:16:32,836 --> 00:16:35,492
- This thing has neutralized
every bit of our equipment.

449
00:16:35,492 --> 00:16:36,929
- [Crow] Even my acting.

450
00:16:36,929 --> 00:16:38,302
- There's not a thing we can do about it.

451
00:16:38,302 --> 00:16:40,016
No way to check speed or position

452
00:16:40,016 --> 00:16:42,022
and not a chance to make
contact with anyone.

453
00:16:42,022 --> 00:16:43,206
- [Tom] It's not fair (whimpers)

454
00:16:43,206 --> 00:16:44,669
- They may have us under robot control.

455
00:16:44,669 --> 00:16:46,855
- I don't know, Vena.

456
00:16:46,855 --> 00:16:48,415
- [Crow] I just don't know.

457
00:16:48,415 --> 00:16:49,870
- I don't know any way of finding out.

458
00:16:49,870 --> 00:16:53,870
- [Joel] Might as well
just fade this scene out.

459
00:16:55,349 --> 00:16:57,179
- [Tom] And this is what
the Heritage Foundation

460
00:16:57,179 --> 00:16:59,929
will look like if you contribute.

461
00:17:01,222 --> 00:17:05,055
- [Tom] Exterminate!
Exterminate! Exterminate!

462
00:17:06,988 --> 00:17:08,984
- [Crow] Sure hope my
support belt holds up.

463
00:17:08,984 --> 00:17:11,184
- Has kept that spaceship
visiograph busy for an hour.

464
00:17:11,184 --> 00:17:13,688
She knew I was going to call.

465
00:17:13,688 --> 00:17:16,336
- Well, she's havin' a vacation, Rocky.

466
00:17:16,336 --> 00:17:19,228
Now, for me, let me relax
with a little black book

467
00:17:19,228 --> 00:17:20,414
and a gay night life.

468
00:17:20,414 --> 00:17:21,630
- [Joel] Uh, insert joke here.

469
00:17:21,630 --> 00:17:22,709
- [Crow] Yeah.

470
00:17:22,709 --> 00:17:25,113
- Well here, relax, Rocky.

471
00:17:25,113 --> 00:17:27,713
I'll give ya a couple of choice pages.

472
00:17:27,713 --> 00:17:28,746
(buzzing)

473
00:17:28,746 --> 00:17:33,683
- [Tom] Mm, here's Christopher,
Trevor, Todd, Kyle...

474
00:17:33,683 --> 00:17:35,306
♫ You're in the Army now

475
00:17:35,306 --> 00:17:37,171
♫ And always get your trout

476
00:17:37,171 --> 00:17:38,526
♫ You'll never get rich but ♫

477
00:17:38,526 --> 00:17:40,116
- I'm glad I found you in, Rocky.

478
00:17:40,116 --> 00:17:41,014
- [Tom] But I'm not in Rocky.

479
00:17:41,014 --> 00:17:42,943
- There's something I'd like to discuss.

480
00:17:42,943 --> 00:17:44,453
If it doesn't upset your plans.

481
00:17:44,453 --> 00:17:46,189
- It won't, sir.

482
00:17:46,189 --> 00:17:47,990
- [Man On Screen] After all,
this is your off duty period.

483
00:17:47,990 --> 00:17:52,157
- [Crow] Oh duh-huh, my black
book, no I won't be able.

484
00:17:55,565 --> 00:17:56,529
- [Joel] You know,

485
00:17:56,529 --> 00:17:58,502
by 1980 everyone will
have phones like this.

486
00:17:58,502 --> 00:17:59,885
- Well I kissed the
beautiful girls goodbye.

487
00:17:59,885 --> 00:18:01,152
- And the gay night life.

488
00:18:01,152 --> 00:18:02,411
- And the gay night life.

489
00:18:02,411 --> 00:18:03,582
- [Tom] Ack, so, his hinnie...

490
00:18:03,582 --> 00:18:05,999
- [Crow] Well, oh never mind.

491
00:18:14,565 --> 00:18:17,482
- [Tom] Look out, ready for ground.

492
00:18:18,810 --> 00:18:19,974
- Well, that's alright, sir.

493
00:18:19,974 --> 00:18:23,489
I can take care of cancelling
our vacations plans, I guess.

494
00:18:23,489 --> 00:18:24,990
- [Joel] Enhancing your vacation?

495
00:18:24,990 --> 00:18:27,299
- Perhaps I should assign
someone else to the mission?

496
00:18:27,299 --> 00:18:28,519
- [Crow] How about Major Heating?

497
00:18:28,519 --> 00:18:31,478
- That's right, we'd rather
ride the rocket, sir.

498
00:18:31,478 --> 00:18:32,311
- [Tom] What does he--

499
00:18:32,311 --> 00:18:33,692
- [Joel] Shhhhh.

500
00:18:33,692 --> 00:18:37,781
- I don't know where this
problem is going to lead.

501
00:18:37,781 --> 00:18:39,980
- [Tom] I don't know how to looooove.

502
00:18:39,980 --> 00:18:42,562
- [Joel] (fart sounds)

503
00:18:42,562 --> 00:18:43,644
- Well sir, you know us.

504
00:18:43,644 --> 00:18:46,116
We're not happy unless we're in trouble.

505
00:18:46,116 --> 00:18:47,413
I mean.

506
00:18:47,413 --> 00:18:49,399
- [Tom] Heh, heh. Get out! Get out!

507
00:18:49,399 --> 00:18:52,983
- First I'll fill you in
on some of the details.

508
00:18:52,983 --> 00:18:54,162
- [Crow] I've prepared a song.

509
00:18:54,162 --> 00:18:56,090
- The United Worlds, as you know,

510
00:18:56,090 --> 00:18:59,028
are fortifying the planetoid, Casa 7.

511
00:18:59,028 --> 00:19:02,360
As a joint control station
for our entire solar system.

512
00:19:02,360 --> 00:19:03,664
- [Crow] I, did not know that.

513
00:19:03,664 --> 00:19:04,497
- Oh yes.

514
00:19:04,497 --> 00:19:06,016
Professor Newton told us
something about the project.

515
00:19:06,016 --> 00:19:08,334
- In preparing Casa 7,
each of the United Worlds

516
00:19:08,334 --> 00:19:10,970
is furnishing strategic,
and in most cases,

517
00:19:10,970 --> 00:19:13,110
restricted materials.

518
00:19:13,110 --> 00:19:14,479
- [Joel] And they're
releasing it to teens.

519
00:19:14,479 --> 00:19:16,247
- [Drake] But lately there
have been disturbing reports

520
00:19:16,247 --> 00:19:20,123
of cargo spaceships vanishing
on the way to Casa 7.

521
00:19:20,123 --> 00:19:21,892
(buzzing)

522
00:19:21,892 --> 00:19:23,027
- [Joel] At beneficial,

523
00:19:23,027 --> 00:19:23,860
- [Tom] Doot doot.

524
00:19:23,860 --> 00:19:25,593
- [Joel] You're good for more.

525
00:19:25,593 --> 00:19:27,160
- We're in contact by
visiograph with Mars, sir.

526
00:19:27,160 --> 00:19:28,527
They request Secretary Drake.

527
00:19:28,527 --> 00:19:30,577
- I'll take it on my receiver.

528
00:19:30,577 --> 00:19:32,003
- [Crow] 'Scuse me boys,
I have to take this.

529
00:19:32,003 --> 00:19:32,890
You understand.

530
00:19:32,890 --> 00:19:34,293
- [Tom] Bah doo doo doo.

531
00:19:34,293 --> 00:19:37,113
There's my Lichtenstein.

532
00:19:37,113 --> 00:19:41,596
- [Joel] Mork calling
Orson, Mork calling Orson.

533
00:19:41,596 --> 00:19:43,819
- Speaking from Mars, Ruinus here.

534
00:19:43,819 --> 00:19:47,420
This is the final report
on our supply spaceship,

535
00:19:47,420 --> 00:19:49,287
Double M en-route to Casa 7.

536
00:19:49,287 --> 00:19:51,984
It is now two Moon cycles over due.

537
00:19:51,984 --> 00:19:52,817
- [Tom] I'm so ashamed.

538
00:19:52,817 --> 00:19:54,860
- [Ruinus] We must presume it to be lost.

539
00:19:54,860 --> 00:19:57,570
- [Drake] Space Rangers are
being assigned immediately.

540
00:19:57,570 --> 00:20:01,148
To investigate the entire
situation of missing cargo ships.

541
00:20:01,148 --> 00:20:03,816
- I know you'll keep us
informed, Mr. Secretary.

542
00:20:03,816 --> 00:20:06,122
- [Drake] You'll have a
report within a solar month.

543
00:20:06,122 --> 00:20:08,238
Greetings from Earth, Ruinus.

544
00:20:08,238 --> 00:20:09,597
- Greetings from Mars--

545
00:20:09,597 --> 00:20:11,316
- [Joel] Ciao baby, right back at 'cha.

546
00:20:11,316 --> 00:20:15,316
- [Crow] What a jerk,
sorry you had to see that.

547
00:20:16,478 --> 00:20:17,895
- You heard.

548
00:20:17,895 --> 00:20:20,931
That's the third spaceship
vanished within a week.

549
00:20:20,931 --> 00:20:23,008
- You know of course, sir,
that Vena's on her way

550
00:20:23,008 --> 00:20:24,991
to Casa 7 on a cargo ship.

551
00:20:24,991 --> 00:20:25,824
- That's right, sir.

552
00:20:25,824 --> 00:20:27,271
Rocky's been trying to call Vena.

553
00:20:27,271 --> 00:20:28,483
- I've been unable to make contact.

554
00:20:28,483 --> 00:20:31,023
And frankly, sir, I'm a bit worried.

555
00:20:31,023 --> 00:20:32,349
- We'll put your mind at ease.

556
00:20:32,349 --> 00:20:33,182
- [Joel] I've got somethin'

557
00:20:33,182 --> 00:20:36,095
that'll put you through the floor, boys.

558
00:20:36,095 --> 00:20:37,012
- Egans.

559
00:20:37,012 --> 00:20:37,845
- [Tom] Send in the clowns!

560
00:20:37,845 --> 00:20:39,362
Don't bother, they're here.

561
00:20:39,362 --> 00:20:44,245
- I want to know if cargo
spaceship CM7 has landed.

562
00:20:44,245 --> 00:20:45,830
- [Joel] And bring me
some sleepy-time tea.

563
00:20:45,830 --> 00:20:49,804
- We want to find out what's
happening to the cargo ships.

564
00:20:49,804 --> 00:20:51,763
- Oh, I'm sure it can be done, sir.

565
00:20:51,763 --> 00:20:53,047
By using our space stations.

566
00:20:53,047 --> 00:20:53,880
- [Crow] Scott Tracy.

567
00:20:53,880 --> 00:20:55,829
Hmm, less animated.

568
00:20:55,829 --> 00:20:58,412
- We've got to find the answer.

569
00:20:59,300 --> 00:21:01,216
Or there'll be repercussions throughout

570
00:21:01,216 --> 00:21:02,049
our entire system.

571
00:21:02,049 --> 00:21:02,882
- [Crow] Chin, get Danno,

572
00:21:02,882 --> 00:21:04,030
round up every known hood on the island.

573
00:21:04,030 --> 00:21:05,588
- The report from Casa 7, sir.

574
00:21:05,588 --> 00:21:06,421
- Let's have it.

575
00:21:06,421 --> 00:21:09,177
- [Tom] It says, "Haaaaaaaaaaalp!"

576
00:21:09,177 --> 00:21:10,783
- Last heard from as it was about to enter

577
00:21:10,783 --> 00:21:12,336
the gravity field for the approach.

578
00:21:12,336 --> 00:21:13,696
Since then there's been no word--

579
00:21:13,696 --> 00:21:14,721
- [Joel] Man does this ever bite,

580
00:21:14,721 --> 00:21:16,755
I need a career change. (disgusted sound)

581
00:21:16,755 --> 00:21:19,703
- CM7 has disappeared into space.

582
00:21:19,703 --> 00:21:20,820
- Thank you--

583
00:21:20,820 --> 00:21:21,908
- [Tom] It was very
good, very good indeed.

584
00:21:21,908 --> 00:21:23,543
Thank you, thank you, very good.

585
00:21:23,543 --> 00:21:26,512
- I'd like to start by
tracing spaceship CM7.

586
00:21:26,512 --> 00:21:28,544
- Of course, this
mission is in your hands.

587
00:21:28,544 --> 00:21:30,230
- Good, we can blast off within the hour.

588
00:21:30,230 --> 00:21:31,063
Winky.

589
00:21:32,422 --> 00:21:37,047
- [Tom] I wonder if Winky
has a nickname. Hah!

590
00:21:37,047 --> 00:21:39,231
- Get the Orbit Jet ready
for blastoff, Winky.

591
00:21:39,231 --> 00:21:41,419
I'm going to see Professor
Newton for a moment.

592
00:21:41,419 --> 00:21:43,111
- The rockets'll be ready to roar.

593
00:21:43,111 --> 00:21:46,444
- [Tom] Oh I'd like to slap him so hard.

594
00:21:48,483 --> 00:21:49,994
- [Joel] Kids, close that door.

595
00:21:49,994 --> 00:21:51,743
We're not trying to heat the outside.

596
00:21:51,743 --> 00:21:52,624
Come on.

597
00:21:52,624 --> 00:21:55,765
- [Crow] And that's how
cattle are inseminated.

598
00:21:55,765 --> 00:21:57,352
Eh-tao-oo-bovine.

599
00:21:57,352 --> 00:21:59,924
- Now we'll have to give this at least

600
00:21:59,924 --> 00:22:02,195
a four hour exposure, Bobby.

601
00:22:02,195 --> 00:22:04,252
- Well that's the longest one yet.

602
00:22:04,252 --> 00:22:05,197
- [Joel] How come you don't

603
00:22:05,197 --> 00:22:08,107
have to wear stretch pants, grandpa?

604
00:22:08,107 --> 00:22:11,358
- Oh Rocky, we're making some
wonderful pictures of Scorpus.

605
00:22:11,358 --> 00:22:12,378
With hyrdrogen--

606
00:22:12,378 --> 00:22:13,453
- [Tom] Yeah, that's great.

607
00:22:13,453 --> 00:22:16,203
- What we need are some
trick snapshots of Casa 7.

608
00:22:16,203 --> 00:22:18,551
- Your tone tells me there's trouble.

609
00:22:18,551 --> 00:22:19,384
- Perhaps.

610
00:22:20,767 --> 00:22:22,757
But I don't know what it is, professor.

611
00:22:22,757 --> 00:22:25,277
- Accept that it concerns Casa 7.

612
00:22:25,277 --> 00:22:26,415
- [Tom] Vladimir Horowitz.

613
00:22:26,415 --> 00:22:28,249
- Secretary Drake will
tell you the whole story.

614
00:22:28,249 --> 00:22:30,434
This much I wanted you to know.

615
00:22:30,434 --> 00:22:32,163
- [Tom] (gibberish)

616
00:22:32,163 --> 00:22:34,231
- The ship Vena's on,
has vanished into space.

617
00:22:34,231 --> 00:22:35,778
- I wanna help, Rocky.

618
00:22:35,778 --> 00:22:37,167
Please let me help.

619
00:22:37,167 --> 00:22:40,381
- This is one time I'd
like to say no, Bobby.

620
00:22:40,381 --> 00:22:41,909
But, I can't.

621
00:22:41,909 --> 00:22:42,916
- [Crow] You outrank me.

622
00:22:42,916 --> 00:22:44,412
- Thanks a million.

623
00:22:44,412 --> 00:22:45,913
You won't be sorry.

624
00:22:45,913 --> 00:22:47,286
We'll find Vena.

625
00:22:47,286 --> 00:22:49,203
- [Tom] I'm already sorry, Bobby.

626
00:22:49,203 --> 00:22:50,187
- Now, run along and get packed.

627
00:22:50,187 --> 00:22:51,935
Meet us at the blastoff platform.

628
00:22:51,935 --> 00:22:56,118
- [Crow] Not a word of
our meetings, Bobby.

629
00:22:56,118 --> 00:22:57,295
- Professor Newton.

630
00:22:57,295 --> 00:22:59,147
- [Joel] How are the fig
cookies coming along.

631
00:22:59,147 --> 00:23:01,150
- I don't know where this
flight is going to take us.

632
00:23:01,150 --> 00:23:03,271
Maybe to the far limits
of our solar system.

633
00:23:03,271 --> 00:23:05,134
- [Crow] Maybe to the
darkest reaches of our souls.

634
00:23:05,134 --> 00:23:06,690
- Something you wish to ask me, Rocky?

635
00:23:06,690 --> 00:23:07,523
- Yes--

636
00:23:07,523 --> 00:23:08,592
- [Tom] Have you ever
danced with the devil

637
00:23:08,592 --> 00:23:09,574
in the pale moonlight?

638
00:23:09,574 --> 00:23:10,956
- Any new discoveries still held secret

639
00:23:10,956 --> 00:23:12,539
that might help us?

640
00:23:13,548 --> 00:23:14,881
- Yes, there is.

641
00:23:16,171 --> 00:23:19,035
But I've been fearful
of even discussing it.

642
00:23:19,035 --> 00:23:19,921
- [Crow] Except with Bobby.

643
00:23:19,921 --> 00:23:22,921
- It could have cataclysmic results.

644
00:23:23,917 --> 00:23:26,062
- Vena's life may be at stake.

645
00:23:26,062 --> 00:23:27,280
- [Joel] You want to go?

646
00:23:27,280 --> 00:23:28,494
- [Tom] Come on, let's go let's go.

647
00:23:28,494 --> 00:23:29,490
- [Crow] Okay.

648
00:23:29,490 --> 00:23:33,985
- I'll show you, I'll show
you the power of cold light.

649
00:23:33,985 --> 00:23:35,068
- Cold light?

650
00:23:47,838 --> 00:23:51,395
- Peggy, I'm afraid I have
some bad news for you.

651
00:23:51,395 --> 00:23:52,580
- Oh my God!

652
00:23:52,580 --> 00:23:53,590
What is it?

653
00:23:53,590 --> 00:23:55,437
Is it a hiatus hernia?

654
00:23:55,437 --> 00:23:57,832
- No, it's not that.

655
00:23:57,832 --> 00:24:00,120
- Is it the heart break of psoriasis?

656
00:24:00,120 --> 00:24:02,369
- No, it's not that.

657
00:24:02,369 --> 00:24:04,570
- Is it Mogo on the Ga-go-go?

658
00:24:04,570 --> 00:24:07,031
- No, I'm afraid it's
much worse than that.

659
00:24:07,031 --> 00:24:08,000
- Oh please, Doc.

660
00:24:08,000 --> 00:24:09,150
Tell me what it is!

661
00:24:09,150 --> 00:24:10,918
- Well it seems that when you were walking

662
00:24:10,918 --> 00:24:13,700
down the hall earlier, the
back of hospital gown was open

663
00:24:13,700 --> 00:24:16,076
and everyone could see your butt!

664
00:24:16,076 --> 00:24:19,585
- I'll never live down the shame!

665
00:24:19,585 --> 00:24:22,279
- You know, my dear, in
tough situations like this

666
00:24:22,279 --> 00:24:24,875
I've found in the past that
the best thing a patient can do

667
00:24:24,875 --> 00:24:28,292
is be comforted by me, Dr. Chad Feelgood.

668
00:24:29,188 --> 00:24:30,021
- You cad!

669
00:24:30,892 --> 00:24:33,376
I knew you were cheating on me!

670
00:24:33,376 --> 00:24:37,085
I hate you, I hate you, I hate you!

671
00:24:37,085 --> 00:24:38,589
Hey, nice bod.

672
00:24:38,589 --> 00:24:41,658
- I'll never live down the (crying)

673
00:24:41,658 --> 00:24:44,288
- Oh Peggy, I can comfort you with--

674
00:24:44,288 --> 00:24:46,976
- Hey, wait and say what's going on here?

675
00:24:46,976 --> 00:24:47,809
- Oh no!

676
00:24:47,809 --> 00:24:48,981
It's Dr. Joel Robinson,

677
00:24:48,981 --> 00:24:50,121
the hard-drinking, two-fisted,

678
00:24:50,121 --> 00:24:52,980
cantankerous yet lovable
hospital administrator!

679
00:24:52,980 --> 00:24:54,217
- I am not.

680
00:24:54,217 --> 00:24:55,050
(all gasp)

681
00:24:55,050 --> 00:24:57,055
- Oh no, and he's suffering from amnesia!

682
00:24:57,055 --> 00:24:58,682
Oh the pain and the misery.

683
00:24:58,682 --> 00:25:01,128
- You guys, I'm not gonna
play soap opera with you.

684
00:25:01,128 --> 00:25:03,103
When I was nine years
old, my sister made me

685
00:25:03,103 --> 00:25:05,122
play soap opera, I'm not
gonna play soap opera.

686
00:25:05,122 --> 00:25:06,622
I won't play soap opera.

687
00:25:06,622 --> 00:25:08,539
Okay Cambot, that's it.

688
00:25:09,448 --> 00:25:10,281
That's it.

689
00:25:10,281 --> 00:25:11,864
Alright, that's it.

690
00:25:12,973 --> 00:25:13,890
Who's next?

691
00:25:20,506 --> 00:25:21,431
- They must of seen us.

692
00:25:21,431 --> 00:25:23,261
- [Tom] Thanks a lot, Joel.

693
00:25:23,261 --> 00:25:24,736
- [Crow] Yeah.

694
00:25:24,736 --> 00:25:27,590
- It may of come from Casa 7.

695
00:25:27,590 --> 00:25:29,923
- Well you'll soon find out.

696
00:25:31,000 --> 00:25:35,167
(Crow and Tom honking and beeping)

697
00:25:40,513 --> 00:25:42,260
- Can they come along side us?

698
00:25:42,260 --> 00:25:44,959
- Yes, I'm sure the
magnetic locks in operation.

699
00:25:44,959 --> 00:25:48,709
- [Crow] Wow, that was
better than I thought!

700
00:25:49,872 --> 00:25:52,084
- Probably aligning the airlock hatch.

701
00:25:52,084 --> 00:25:54,317
- [Joel] It's an old
lady, she rear-ended 'em.

702
00:25:54,317 --> 00:25:55,910
- [Crow] What are they doing, Joel?

703
00:25:55,910 --> 00:25:56,979
- [Joel] They're telling secrets.

704
00:25:56,979 --> 00:25:58,833
- [Crow] Ahh.

705
00:25:58,833 --> 00:25:59,748
- They've breached the hatch.

706
00:25:59,748 --> 00:26:01,415
We're connected now.

707
00:26:02,405 --> 00:26:03,312
- [Tom] Oh, hang on a minute.

708
00:26:03,312 --> 00:26:07,310
Gotta put my head in the salad spinner.

709
00:26:07,310 --> 00:26:10,831
- [Crow] Oh he didn't
even turn the handle!

710
00:26:10,831 --> 00:26:14,748
- [Tom] My, what a cheap
crummy special effect.

711
00:26:16,658 --> 00:26:18,346
- [Joel] Blondie, I'm home.

712
00:26:18,346 --> 00:26:21,127
I brought Mr. Dithers along.

713
00:26:21,127 --> 00:26:22,196
- [Joel] (sighs)

714
00:26:22,196 --> 00:26:23,689
- [Crow] Boy I told you to find adventure,

715
00:26:23,689 --> 00:26:26,092
not bring it home with you.

716
00:26:26,092 --> 00:26:28,462
- [Joel] Hi, can I be
submissive for anyone?

717
00:26:28,462 --> 00:26:30,295
- Are you from Casa 7?

718
00:26:31,357 --> 00:26:33,043
- [Joel] I can if you want me to be.

719
00:26:33,043 --> 00:26:35,750
- On Casa 7 they don't
even know you're alive.

720
00:26:35,750 --> 00:26:37,419
- Then you're the ones who
neutralized our equipment.

721
00:26:37,419 --> 00:26:40,523
- You're real bright to
figure that out for yourself.

722
00:26:40,523 --> 00:26:41,978
- [Crow] Thanks! That's
nice of you to--Hey!

723
00:26:41,978 --> 00:26:44,228
- Relax, it won't be alive.

724
00:26:45,497 --> 00:26:48,080
- [Tom] Uhm, anyone for coffee?

725
00:26:49,103 --> 00:26:52,522
- [Crow] I'll just wait here then.

726
00:26:52,522 --> 00:26:54,433
- [Tom] Psst, hey buddy.

727
00:26:54,433 --> 00:26:55,747
- [Joel] Hey, check this out.

728
00:26:55,747 --> 00:26:57,723
There's a ton of cool stuff in here.

729
00:26:57,723 --> 00:27:01,576
Oh cool you don't even have
to push any buttons to get in.

730
00:27:01,576 --> 00:27:04,380
This is, oh man, this is where
they store their costumes.

731
00:27:04,380 --> 00:27:07,963
These fantastic VCRs,
Nintendo, it's great.

732
00:27:10,172 --> 00:27:11,755
- [Tom] Ooh, fudge.

733
00:27:15,236 --> 00:27:19,277
- [Crow] I'll throw this
caramelled apple at him.

734
00:27:19,277 --> 00:27:23,366
- [Joel] Foo-di-doo,
nothing behind my back.

735
00:27:23,366 --> 00:27:24,283
- [Tom] Hi.

736
00:27:28,204 --> 00:27:30,038
- [Crow] A little song, a little grace,

737
00:27:30,038 --> 00:27:32,538
a little seltzer in your face.

738
00:27:34,675 --> 00:27:36,596
- [Tom] Take that, ha ha ha.

739
00:27:36,596 --> 00:27:39,994
Casa 7, love it or leave it, buddy.

740
00:27:39,994 --> 00:27:42,129
- [Joel] They're gonna
play the limbo real low.

741
00:27:42,129 --> 00:27:44,471
- [Tom] Think it's played
by Trip Shakespeare.

742
00:27:44,471 --> 00:27:46,721
(laughter)

743
00:27:48,798 --> 00:27:49,642
- Vena, your space gun.

744
00:27:49,642 --> 00:27:50,476
- [Crow] What about it?

745
00:27:50,476 --> 00:27:52,643
Oh, I should get it, okay.

746
00:27:53,792 --> 00:27:54,625
- If you have to, use it.

747
00:27:54,625 --> 00:27:55,943
Ask questions later.

748
00:27:55,943 --> 00:28:00,133
I'll get through to Casa 7 on
the astrophone on their ship.

749
00:28:00,133 --> 00:28:02,065
- [Crow] But if I shoot
'em, I can't ask questions.

750
00:28:02,065 --> 00:28:03,410
- [Tom] No you see,
it's a figure of speech.

751
00:28:03,410 --> 00:28:04,743
- [Crow] Ah, oh.

752
00:28:07,238 --> 00:28:08,100
I know what you're thinking.

753
00:28:08,100 --> 00:28:11,600
Did I shoot six shots of seltzer or seven?

754
00:28:15,210 --> 00:28:19,155
- [Joel] Alright, hand
me that terrarium, now.

755
00:28:19,155 --> 00:28:20,738
- [Crow] Ooh, ouch.

756
00:28:22,574 --> 00:28:24,574
Wellll, Mrs. Carmichael?

757
00:28:29,841 --> 00:28:30,796
- Go over there.

758
00:28:30,796 --> 00:28:32,399
- [Joel] Okay, now bark like a dog.

759
00:28:32,399 --> 00:28:35,816
And you start chewing the other ones leg.

760
00:28:38,835 --> 00:28:40,179
- Now, Vena, you'll drop it.

761
00:28:40,179 --> 00:28:43,346
- [Tom] He's doing a grand jete, look.

762
00:28:44,791 --> 00:28:46,208
- Get over there.

763
00:28:48,779 --> 00:28:49,614
- Nice work.

764
00:28:49,614 --> 00:28:52,784
- [Tom] If you can get
it, then you can get it.

765
00:28:52,784 --> 00:28:54,636
- Only, you don't have any brains.

766
00:28:54,636 --> 00:28:56,779
Now see if you can get their cargo

767
00:28:56,779 --> 00:28:58,859
into our ship without tripping over it.

768
00:28:58,859 --> 00:29:00,472
- [Joel] But you just said we were smart.

769
00:29:00,472 --> 00:29:01,555
Oh, I get it.

770
00:29:04,204 --> 00:29:05,621
- [Crow] Awkward.

771
00:29:08,340 --> 00:29:09,907
- So, Rinkman.

772
00:29:09,907 --> 00:29:12,783
You've ended up as a space pirate.

773
00:29:12,783 --> 00:29:14,792
At least you can't sink any lower.

774
00:29:14,792 --> 00:29:17,203
- [Joel] Well, I could date you.

775
00:29:17,203 --> 00:29:18,057
- Don't you get it?

776
00:29:18,057 --> 00:29:20,057
You destroy space ships.

777
00:29:21,549 --> 00:29:24,053
- [Joel] Hey, it's the sucker brothers.

778
00:29:24,053 --> 00:29:27,206
- [Tom] You know, I saw a college kid

779
00:29:27,206 --> 00:29:29,286
stick his head in a party bowl one time.

780
00:29:29,286 --> 00:29:30,597
- You won't be harmed.

781
00:29:30,597 --> 00:29:33,715
We just neutralized you
ship's rockets and equipment.

782
00:29:33,715 --> 00:29:34,548
- [Crow] And your stomach acid.

783
00:29:34,548 --> 00:29:35,776
- Why are we still in normal flight?

784
00:29:35,776 --> 00:29:37,668
- You're not.

785
00:29:37,668 --> 00:29:41,077
You're revolving around
Casa 7 in a fixed orbit.

786
00:29:41,077 --> 00:29:44,226
Just like the Moon
revolves around the Earth.

787
00:29:44,226 --> 00:29:45,157
- How?

788
00:29:45,157 --> 00:29:47,946
- We cut your power and
neutralized your equipment.

789
00:29:47,946 --> 00:29:49,250
- [Tom] And pass the savings on to you.

790
00:29:49,250 --> 00:29:51,879
- Balanced against the gravity of Casa 7.

791
00:29:51,879 --> 00:29:54,567
- That's what happened to the
other ships you've pirated.

792
00:29:54,567 --> 00:29:55,976
- [Tom] Grrr.
- [Rinkman] That's right.

793
00:29:55,976 --> 00:29:58,070
- You'll be revolving around Casa 7

794
00:29:58,070 --> 00:30:00,104
for the next million years.

795
00:30:00,104 --> 00:30:03,141
Or until a piece of meteoric
waste hits the ship.

796
00:30:03,141 --> 00:30:05,489
- [Joel] Or until I
turn into Robert Stack.

797
00:30:05,489 --> 00:30:09,098
- I'll have the markings
removed from your ship.

798
00:30:09,098 --> 00:30:11,878
- You have found a new
way to commit murder.

799
00:30:11,878 --> 00:30:12,711
- [Tom] You noticed.

800
00:30:12,711 --> 00:30:14,169
- Don't give me any credit, Vena.

801
00:30:14,169 --> 00:30:16,044
Dr. Vanko worked it out.

802
00:30:16,044 --> 00:30:19,913
I just make sure that no
other spaceship bothers you.

803
00:30:19,913 --> 00:30:22,663
- [Crow] Why you, you person you.

804
00:30:24,473 --> 00:30:26,973
- [Joel] There goes a narwhal!

805
00:30:29,445 --> 00:30:31,837
- [Tom] Oh, our air isn't
good enough for the Johnsons.

806
00:30:31,837 --> 00:30:34,981
They have to bring their own.

807
00:30:34,981 --> 00:30:36,017
- [Joel] It's a boy.

808
00:30:36,017 --> 00:30:38,284
- It's the last of it.

809
00:30:38,284 --> 00:30:39,847
- I'll send your pilot back.

810
00:30:39,847 --> 00:30:40,694
- [Tom] You don't have to yell,

811
00:30:40,694 --> 00:30:42,118
I'm sitting right next to you.

812
00:30:42,118 --> 00:30:43,869
- Oh, I almost forgot.

813
00:30:43,869 --> 00:30:44,704
- [Joel] Your dad called.

814
00:30:44,704 --> 00:30:46,855
- In case you're expecting
help from Rocky Jones,

815
00:30:46,855 --> 00:30:47,688
forget it.

816
00:30:47,688 --> 00:30:50,596
I've got a decoy
spaceship waiting for him.

817
00:30:50,596 --> 00:30:53,598
The Orbit Jet will be blown to bits.

818
00:30:53,598 --> 00:30:57,765
- [Crow] Ha ha ha, I can't
pretend I'm not enjoying this.

819
00:31:01,121 --> 00:31:04,350
- [Joel] Orbit Jet is go
- [Tom] Blown to bits

820
00:31:04,350 --> 00:31:07,993
- [Joel] Craw, craw
- [Tom] Bits, blown, bits.

821
00:31:07,993 --> 00:31:09,667
- [Tom] So, uh, which ship is theirs?

822
00:31:09,667 --> 00:31:10,882
The phallic one or the phallic one?

823
00:31:10,882 --> 00:31:14,799
- [Joel] Oh I think it's
the phallic one, oooh.

824
00:31:16,730 --> 00:31:17,563
- [Crow] We'll call ya.

825
00:31:17,563 --> 00:31:18,838
Thanks for breakfast.

826
00:31:18,838 --> 00:31:20,505
- [Tom] Oh boy, now.

827
00:31:21,712 --> 00:31:23,473
- [Joel] Way to go, Bob.

828
00:31:23,473 --> 00:31:25,729
- Do we have a chance?

829
00:31:25,729 --> 00:31:28,542
- No use kidding ourselves, Vena.

830
00:31:28,542 --> 00:31:31,068
It's like a million to one
shot we'll ever be seen.

831
00:31:31,068 --> 00:31:32,280
- [Crow] Oh, they're on Comedy Central.

832
00:31:32,280 --> 00:31:36,197
- Like finding a tiny
fragment in infinite space.

833
00:31:36,197 --> 00:31:38,064
- Until our food gives out.

834
00:31:38,064 --> 00:31:40,122
Or a meteorite hits us.

835
00:31:40,122 --> 00:31:41,882
- That's the deal, Vena.

836
00:31:41,882 --> 00:31:44,594
- [Tom] Vena, when I go I want
you to roast me and eat me.

837
00:31:44,594 --> 00:31:46,240
All of it, brisket too.

838
00:31:46,240 --> 00:31:48,213
- I'll get lunch.

839
00:31:48,213 --> 00:31:51,434
- [Joel] Hazel, will you
cook up something for dinner?

840
00:31:51,434 --> 00:31:53,017
- [Tom] Okay Mr. B.

841
00:32:00,685 --> 00:32:02,702
- Winky, what's our position?

842
00:32:02,702 --> 00:32:05,285
- [Crow] Leaning towards Perot.

843
00:32:07,688 --> 00:32:09,033
- No, let me see if I can read it.

844
00:32:09,033 --> 00:32:10,480
- [Joel] Eh, you have to be 18, kid.

845
00:32:10,480 --> 00:32:11,313
- What are you planning to do?

846
00:32:11,313 --> 00:32:12,387
Get my job as navigator?

847
00:32:12,387 --> 00:32:13,586
- Oh you know I wouldn't take anything

848
00:32:13,586 --> 00:32:14,948
that's yours or Rocky's.

849
00:32:14,948 --> 00:32:16,585
- Alright, go ahead and read it boy.

850
00:32:16,585 --> 00:32:18,141
- [Tom] Yeah, read it boy. Read it!

851
00:32:18,141 --> 00:32:19,084
- [Crow] Do the funny voice.

852
00:32:19,084 --> 00:32:23,558
- Position celestial meridian,
longitude 219 degrees,

853
00:32:23,558 --> 00:32:24,813
20 minutes.

854
00:32:24,813 --> 00:32:25,646
- [Tom] What is this?

855
00:32:25,646 --> 00:32:26,479
Radio AAHS?

856
00:32:26,479 --> 00:32:29,824
- Latitude, 76 degrees, 4 minutes.

857
00:32:29,824 --> 00:32:31,596
- Good work, Bobby.

858
00:32:31,596 --> 00:32:32,544
Oh, Winky?

859
00:32:32,544 --> 00:32:34,474
- [Crow] Jettison Bobby.

860
00:32:34,474 --> 00:32:37,614
- They still have no word
from Vena's spaceship.

861
00:32:37,614 --> 00:32:41,207
- Oh, well maybe we better
start scanning the radar, huh?

862
00:32:41,207 --> 00:32:42,830
- [Tom] What do you think, Bobby?

863
00:32:42,830 --> 00:32:44,869
- Our flight will take us
into Casa's atmosphere.

864
00:32:44,869 --> 00:32:46,446
Hey, Winky?

865
00:32:46,446 --> 00:32:48,838
A spaceship at five o'clock.

866
00:32:48,838 --> 00:32:50,755
- [Crow] Made you look!

867
00:32:52,368 --> 00:32:53,842
- Can you identify it?

868
00:32:53,842 --> 00:32:55,949
- [Tom] Yeah, it's a
spaceship at five o'clock.

869
00:32:55,949 --> 00:32:59,199
- [Winky] Yeah, it's a Mars spaceship.

870
00:33:08,592 --> 00:33:10,339
- I'll arc over the ship at R-400.

871
00:33:10,339 --> 00:33:11,276
- [Tom] Duh, okay.

872
00:33:11,276 --> 00:33:13,400
- Release rocket on count five.

873
00:33:13,400 --> 00:33:14,400
- [Tom] Kay.

874
00:33:16,064 --> 00:33:17,132
- Starting run.

875
00:33:17,132 --> 00:33:17,965
- [Tom] Okay.

876
00:33:17,965 --> 00:33:19,048
- One, two...

877
00:33:20,783 --> 00:33:23,603
- [Crow] What comes after two?

878
00:33:23,603 --> 00:33:24,436
- Three.

879
00:33:24,436 --> 00:33:25,269
- [Crow] Oh.

880
00:33:25,269 --> 00:33:26,102
- Four, Fire!

881
00:33:26,102 --> 00:33:27,519
- [Tom] Hi-keeba!

882
00:33:28,435 --> 00:33:29,268
Ouch.

883
00:33:30,391 --> 00:33:32,906
- Well, the Double M just
became the Scrambled M.

884
00:33:32,906 --> 00:33:34,732
- [Tom] Get out! Get out!

885
00:33:34,732 --> 00:33:36,437
- So then a full report can be sent

886
00:33:36,437 --> 00:33:37,537
to Mars space headquarters.

887
00:33:37,537 --> 00:33:38,733
- [Tom] All done!

888
00:33:38,733 --> 00:33:40,220
- What did'ya hit?

889
00:33:40,220 --> 00:33:42,230
- Sighted enemy, smeared same.

890
00:33:42,230 --> 00:33:44,246
- Why do I have to miss
all the excitement?

891
00:33:44,246 --> 00:33:46,718
- [Crow] 'Cause we don't like
you and you're a bad person.

892
00:33:46,718 --> 00:33:49,200
- Keep the radar vex open, Winky.

893
00:33:49,200 --> 00:33:50,658
I'm sure we're in an area

894
00:33:50,658 --> 00:33:52,766
our unknown enemies
don't want us to search.

895
00:33:52,766 --> 00:33:54,715
- [Tom] Yes, it's a dark forbidden area

896
00:33:54,715 --> 00:33:56,882
full of secrets and shame.

897
00:34:01,199 --> 00:34:02,703
If you'd like to make a call,

898
00:34:02,703 --> 00:34:05,184
please hang up and dial again.

899
00:34:05,184 --> 00:34:07,431
- Rocky, object ahead.

900
00:34:07,431 --> 00:34:10,764
- [Joel] Could you be more vague, Winky?

901
00:34:12,527 --> 00:34:14,576
- Object just about two
solar minutes ahead of us.

902
00:34:14,576 --> 00:34:15,525
- [Crow] Ah, shut up.

903
00:34:15,525 --> 00:34:16,720
What's going on, Winky?

904
00:34:16,720 --> 00:34:17,938
- You're right, Bobby.

905
00:34:17,938 --> 00:34:18,771
Professor Newton can be proud of you.

906
00:34:18,771 --> 00:34:21,235
- Elemental my dear Rocky, elemental.

907
00:34:21,235 --> 00:34:22,461
- [Crow] You little dipstick.

908
00:34:22,461 --> 00:34:24,321
- Winky, when we're half way there

909
00:34:24,321 --> 00:34:27,221
we'll be able to tell if it's a spaceship.

910
00:34:27,221 --> 00:34:28,054
- Rocky?

911
00:34:29,042 --> 00:34:30,970
Why'd you bring this on the Orbit Jet?

912
00:34:30,970 --> 00:34:31,803
- [Tom] Oh that?

913
00:34:31,803 --> 00:34:32,636
That's our Aschenberg.

914
00:34:32,636 --> 00:34:33,613
- That's something Professor Newton's

915
00:34:33,613 --> 00:34:35,010
been working on for a long time.

916
00:34:35,010 --> 00:34:36,691
- I know, it's cold light.

917
00:34:36,691 --> 00:34:39,558
- Oh? Then he's told you about it, huh?

918
00:34:39,558 --> 00:34:41,042
- Yes, we discussed it.

919
00:34:41,042 --> 00:34:42,728
And I gave him my opinion.

920
00:34:42,728 --> 00:34:45,288
- Well I know he appreciated that.

921
00:34:45,288 --> 00:34:48,175
- Cold light should never
be used indiscriminately.

922
00:34:48,175 --> 00:34:50,996
The gamma rays could be
fatal to those who use it.

923
00:34:50,996 --> 00:34:52,568
- [Tom] Remember that, kids.

924
00:34:52,568 --> 00:34:54,591
- Professor Newton warned me.

925
00:34:54,591 --> 00:34:56,360
- Rocky, it's a spaceship ahead.

926
00:34:56,360 --> 00:35:00,003
- [Joel] Has Bobby been giving
you that cold light crap?

927
00:35:00,003 --> 00:35:03,084
- [Tom] Hey, that's us, five minutes ago.

928
00:35:03,084 --> 00:35:04,193
- Safety belts.

929
00:35:04,193 --> 00:35:06,827
- [Joel] 'Cept you, Bobby.

930
00:35:06,827 --> 00:35:08,304
- [Crow] Bobby been getting to you?

931
00:35:08,304 --> 00:35:09,597
You thinking what I'm thinking?

932
00:35:09,597 --> 00:35:11,597
- [Tom] Yup, I've got a headache this big

933
00:35:11,597 --> 00:35:14,227
and it's got Bobby written all over it.

934
00:35:14,227 --> 00:35:17,651
- This is the XV2 calling spaceship

935
00:35:17,651 --> 00:35:21,651
at approximately celestial
meridian 190 degrees.

936
00:35:22,489 --> 00:35:25,156
Celestial parallel 80 degrees.

937
00:35:25,156 --> 00:35:26,403
Come in, identify yourself.

938
00:35:26,403 --> 00:35:28,728
- [Crow] I am Kirok.

939
00:35:28,728 --> 00:35:30,491
- This is the XV2 calling spaceship

940
00:35:30,491 --> 00:35:33,843
at approximately celestial
meridian 180 degrees.

941
00:35:33,843 --> 00:35:37,033
Celestial parallel 90 degrees.

942
00:35:37,033 --> 00:35:38,411
Come in, identify yourself.

943
00:35:38,411 --> 00:35:42,161
- [Tom] I have no idea
what I'm saying, over.

944
00:35:44,259 --> 00:35:46,263
- It's a spaceship, Reggie.

945
00:35:46,263 --> 00:35:47,096
- [Tom] No.

946
00:35:47,096 --> 00:35:48,899
- [Joel] Oh boy, nothing get's passed her.

947
00:35:48,899 --> 00:35:50,870
- We have to get some signal to him.

948
00:35:50,870 --> 00:35:52,212
- We're helpless, Vena.

949
00:35:52,212 --> 00:35:53,879
- The rocket missiles.

950
00:35:53,879 --> 00:35:55,371
- We can't operate the tubes.

951
00:35:55,371 --> 00:35:56,204
- [Crow] I had 'em tied.

952
00:35:56,204 --> 00:35:57,934
- Firing them wouldn't be safe.

953
00:35:57,934 --> 00:35:59,983
- I mean, force them through the tubes.

954
00:35:59,983 --> 00:36:01,477
Drop them over side.

955
00:36:01,477 --> 00:36:03,815
They'd have to see that
and not pass us by.

956
00:36:03,815 --> 00:36:04,648
- It might work.

957
00:36:04,648 --> 00:36:05,481
- [Tom] Who made you the expert?

958
00:36:05,481 --> 00:36:09,648
- We may have enough auxiliary
power to drop them off.

959
00:36:13,690 --> 00:36:14,902
- [Tom] Winky must die!

960
00:36:14,902 --> 00:36:18,264
- Look at their missile tubes, starboard.

961
00:36:18,264 --> 00:36:20,051
- It's starting to open.

962
00:36:20,051 --> 00:36:22,365
- We're gonna be ducking
missiles in a moment.

963
00:36:22,365 --> 00:36:23,440
- Port rocket, Winky.

964
00:36:23,440 --> 00:36:24,273
Same run.

965
00:36:25,767 --> 00:36:27,522
Fire missile on count five.

966
00:36:27,522 --> 00:36:28,759
- Repeat, on five.

967
00:36:28,759 --> 00:36:31,034
- [Joel] Repeat on five, repeat on five.

968
00:36:31,034 --> 00:36:32,867
- [Tom] Look, shut up.

969
00:36:35,751 --> 00:36:36,723
- Starting run.

970
00:36:36,723 --> 00:36:37,556
- Check.

971
00:36:38,399 --> 00:36:40,482
- One, two, three, four--

972
00:36:41,699 --> 00:36:43,641
hold on, Winky, hold fire.

973
00:36:43,641 --> 00:36:46,558
- [Crow] Oh, coughed up a fur-ball.

974
00:36:48,087 --> 00:36:49,476
- They ejected the rocket.

975
00:36:49,476 --> 00:36:51,243
They weren't firing it.

976
00:36:51,243 --> 00:36:52,928
That was meant as a signal to us.

977
00:36:52,928 --> 00:36:55,049
- Maybe the ships in some
kind of trouble, Rocky.

978
00:36:55,049 --> 00:36:56,224
- [Crow] Oh get out of here, Bobby.

979
00:36:56,224 --> 00:36:57,301
Clear the room.

980
00:36:57,301 --> 00:36:58,491
- We're going along side.

981
00:36:58,491 --> 00:36:59,741
- Aye aye, sir.

982
00:37:04,693 --> 00:37:06,953
- The Orbit Jet is gone.

983
00:37:06,953 --> 00:37:09,536
- [All] Stupid car, stupid car!

984
00:37:13,325 --> 00:37:14,431
- [Tom] This is sort of like Diver Dan

985
00:37:14,431 --> 00:37:18,199
only without all the majesty and grandeur.

986
00:37:18,199 --> 00:37:19,293
- [Crow] Look at that effect.

987
00:37:19,293 --> 00:37:22,469
Industrial Light and Magic,
you've done it again!

988
00:37:22,469 --> 00:37:25,036
- [Tom] Oh ho ho ooo.

989
00:37:25,036 --> 00:37:26,156
- It's come along side.

990
00:37:26,156 --> 00:37:27,534
- I'll open the airlock hatch.

991
00:37:27,534 --> 00:37:28,367
- [Joel] Oh great.

992
00:37:28,367 --> 00:37:30,488
It really worked good
last time you did that.

993
00:37:30,488 --> 00:37:33,113
- [Tom] Alright, get on
your mini greenhouse.

994
00:37:33,113 --> 00:37:34,493
- [Crow] I'm turning this wheel.

995
00:37:34,493 --> 00:37:38,493
Really, I'm turning it,
doesn't it look like it?

996
00:37:40,185 --> 00:37:41,825
- [Tom] She waits.

997
00:37:41,825 --> 00:37:43,098
- [Joel] Where have you been?

998
00:37:43,098 --> 00:37:44,765
You could of called.

999
00:37:45,780 --> 00:37:46,870
- [Crow] Oh, hi Bobby, hi Winky.

1000
00:37:46,870 --> 00:37:47,716
- Rocky!

1001
00:37:47,716 --> 00:37:48,549
Bobby!

1002
