1320
00:49:06,117 --> 00:49:07,663
I'll have to brief you on it.

1321
00:49:07,663 --> 00:49:09,721
- [Tom] It's called a
Snuggee. Turn around.

1322
00:49:09,721 --> 00:49:12,851
- The filament in the vacuum
tube is quickly brought

1323
00:49:12,851 --> 00:49:16,994
to a temperature of about
-243 degrees centigrade.

1324
00:49:16,994 --> 00:49:18,906
- [Joel] Ah what was
the middle part again?

1325
00:49:18,906 --> 00:49:22,481
- Well, Professor Newton
explained it this way.

1326
00:49:22,481 --> 00:49:23,431
Heat can effect--

1327
00:49:23,431 --> 00:49:26,287
- [Tom] Blah blah blah
blah blah blah blah.

1328
00:49:26,287 --> 00:49:28,085
Our images, blah blah blah.

1329
00:49:28,085 --> 00:49:29,570
Blah blah seen by blah blah blah.

1330
00:49:29,570 --> 00:49:32,279
Blah blah mirage blah blah blah blah blah.

1331
00:49:32,279 --> 00:49:33,943
- Now intense cold--

1332
00:49:33,943 --> 00:49:36,856
- [Tom] Blah blah, cold, blah blah.

1333
00:49:36,856 --> 00:49:40,354
- [Crow] I'm sorry, I wasn't listening.

1334
00:49:40,354 --> 00:49:42,658
- The ray that is sent out by
the terrifically cold light,

1335
00:49:42,658 --> 00:49:44,873
will make the Orbit Jet invisible.

1336
00:49:44,873 --> 00:49:47,270
- Well how can we fly a ship we can't see?

1337
00:49:47,270 --> 00:49:50,016
- The cold light will surround the ship.

1338
00:49:50,016 --> 00:49:51,106
- [Tom] (scoffs) You idiot.

1339
00:49:51,106 --> 00:49:52,823
- We'll be able to see
everything normally,

1340
00:49:52,823 --> 00:49:53,656
here in the cabins.

1341
00:49:53,656 --> 00:49:55,859
But no one will be able to see us.

1342
00:49:55,859 --> 00:49:58,111
- Well if that can't get us
through any defense barrier,

1343
00:49:58,111 --> 00:49:59,598
nothing can.

1344
00:49:59,598 --> 00:50:01,029
- Oh, just one point, Winky.

1345
00:50:01,029 --> 00:50:01,862
- [Tom] Shut up!

1346
00:50:01,862 --> 00:50:03,151
- We have to fight time.

1347
00:50:03,151 --> 00:50:05,280
We don't know how long the
cold lamp will operate,

1348
00:50:05,280 --> 00:50:07,404
so, stand by to switch it on.

1349
00:50:07,404 --> 00:50:08,487
- [Tom] Okay.

1350
00:50:16,065 --> 00:50:18,813
- [Crow] Hey, it's a Universal film.

1351
00:50:18,813 --> 00:50:20,419
- We're entering Prah's gravity field.

1352
00:50:20,419 --> 00:50:21,703
Switch it on, Winky.

1353
00:50:21,703 --> 00:50:22,870
- [Crow] Okay.

1354
00:50:24,618 --> 00:50:25,717
- [Tom] There, you see, I did it, Rocky.

1355
00:50:25,717 --> 00:50:26,662
I did it, I switched it on.

1356
00:50:26,662 --> 00:50:27,495
How did I do?

1357
00:50:27,495 --> 00:50:28,539
Did I do well?

1358
00:50:28,539 --> 00:50:29,399
I switched it on, I did it.

1359
00:50:29,399 --> 00:50:30,399
I did it, did you see that?

1360
00:50:30,399 --> 00:50:32,899
I switched it on, I can do it.

1361
00:50:38,116 --> 00:50:39,511
- How do you know if the ship's invisible?

1362
00:50:39,511 --> 00:50:40,584
- [Joel] Will I feel invisible?

1363
00:50:40,584 --> 00:50:42,307
- But if something hits us,

1364
00:50:42,307 --> 00:50:44,264
we'll know the cold light didn't work.

1365
00:50:44,264 --> 00:50:47,236
- That's finding out the hard way.

1366
00:50:47,236 --> 00:50:48,811
- [Tom] You don't know the
half of it, little guy.

1367
00:50:48,811 --> 00:50:51,873
- Boy, that's a rugged place.

1368
00:50:51,873 --> 00:50:52,963
- [Crow] That's a Van Gogh.

1369
00:50:52,963 --> 00:50:55,025
- [Tom] Van Gochghgh.

1370
00:50:55,025 --> 00:50:56,232
- Activate the gyro.

1371
00:50:56,232 --> 00:50:58,950
- [Joel] No, it's pronounce ee-ro.

1372
00:50:58,950 --> 00:50:59,975
- Activated, sir.

1373
00:50:59,975 --> 00:51:01,268
- Secure for landing.

1374
00:51:01,268 --> 00:51:02,872
- [Tom] Please put your
seats in their locked,

1375
00:51:02,872 --> 00:51:03,824
upright position.

1376
00:51:03,824 --> 00:51:05,593
- But even if we can spot a
place in the Rocky terrain.

1377
00:51:05,593 --> 00:51:07,328
The Orbit Jet won't stand on it's tail.

1378
00:51:07,328 --> 00:51:09,098
- [Joel] Don't start with me, Winky.

1379
00:51:09,098 --> 00:51:11,813
- We'll arrive on one of
their landing platforms.

1380
00:51:11,813 --> 00:51:14,921
- Well, somebody's gonna be surprised.

1381
00:51:14,921 --> 00:51:16,504
I hope it isn't us.

1382
00:51:19,055 --> 00:51:21,841
- [Tom] You hear an
invisible ship just now?

1383
00:51:21,841 --> 00:51:24,211
- Who could possibly land on Prah?

1384
00:51:24,211 --> 00:51:25,609
- Marcov?
- [Tom] Polo.

1385
00:51:25,609 --> 00:51:26,442
Marcov!

1386
00:51:26,442 --> 00:51:27,275
- [Tom] Polo!

1387
00:51:27,275 --> 00:51:28,108
- [Voiceover] Markov here.

1388
00:51:28,108 --> 00:51:29,319
