is at one of the platforms.

1980
01:12:58,938 --> 01:13:00,054
- [Tom] At a cool temperature.

1981
01:13:00,054 --> 01:13:03,198
- Oh have you seen anything of Hagar Nu?

1982
01:13:03,198 --> 01:13:04,672
- Not a sign.

1983
01:13:04,672 --> 01:13:07,201
- [Tom] Stop accusing me!

1984
01:13:07,201 --> 01:13:10,284
- [Crow] Shoes for industry, comrade.

1985
01:13:11,485 --> 01:13:14,366
- [Tom] Oh wait, I forgot
to validate your parking.

1986
01:13:14,366 --> 01:13:18,366
- [Joel] Ken is that close
to a written warning.

1987
01:13:19,855 --> 01:13:24,420
- [Crow] Oh, he's gonna
do the Letterman thing.

1988
01:13:24,420 --> 01:13:27,564
- [Tom] Top of the gantry, ma!

1989
01:13:27,564 --> 01:13:29,645
- [Crow] And they're gone, huzzah!

1990
01:13:29,645 --> 01:13:34,329
- [Joel] They're really proud
of that process, aren't they?

1991
01:13:34,329 --> 01:13:38,360
- [Crow] Mom, I found a
spaceman, can I keep him?

1992
01:13:38,360 --> 01:13:42,193
- [Joel] Okay, now you
two play nice together.

1993
01:13:43,886 --> 01:13:44,911
- [Tom] I think you two will get along.

1994
01:13:44,911 --> 01:13:46,994
Rocky's into science too.

1995
01:13:51,974 --> 01:13:52,991
- [Crow] Good morning sunshine.

1996
01:13:52,991 --> 01:13:54,408
- [Joel] Trotsky?

1997
01:13:57,083 --> 01:14:00,812
- Did you also catch up
with the traitor Ken?

1998
01:14:00,812 --> 01:14:02,423
- [Tom] Uh, hm, yeah, sure.

1999
01:14:02,423 --> 01:14:03,612
- So it was Ken.

2000
01:14:03,612 --> 01:14:05,025
- [Joel] Jeeze I hate that guy Ken.

2001
01:14:05,025 --> 01:14:07,014
- I guess both of us found out too late.

2002
01:14:07,014 --> 01:14:09,066
- You are an Earth man.

2003
01:14:09,066 --> 01:14:11,451
- Yes, Rocky Jones, I
command the Orbit Jet.

2004
01:14:11,451 --> 01:14:13,701
- I am Hagar Nu, a Martian.

2005
01:14:14,795 --> 01:14:16,811
- They're looking for you as the traitor.

2006
01:14:16,811 --> 01:14:18,880
- Ken arranged that, cleverly.

2007
01:14:18,880 --> 01:14:22,277
After I caught him giving
information to the pirates.

2008
01:14:22,277 --> 01:14:24,857
He had to silence me.

2009
01:14:24,857 --> 01:14:26,899
- Yes, he's quite a hand at that.

2010
01:14:26,899 --> 01:14:29,889
- For two days I was bound and helpless

2011
01:14:29,889 --> 01:14:32,261
in the charting room at central station.

2012
01:14:32,261 --> 01:14:34,007
- [Crow] It wasn't that bad, really.

2013
01:14:34,007 --> 01:14:37,904
- I was into a deep sleep
and found myself here.

2014
01:14:37,904 --> 01:14:40,001
- [Tom] Oh yeah, Winky sang to you too?

2015
01:14:40,001 --> 01:14:41,611
- We're on my ship, the Orbit Jet.

2016
01:14:41,611 --> 01:14:43,460
That's where Ken made his mistake.

2017
01:14:43,460 --> 01:14:45,321
I know this ship too well.

2018
01:14:45,321 --> 01:14:47,607
- Ken is an evil man.

2019
01:14:47,607 --> 01:14:49,114
He'll not stop--

2020
01:14:49,114 --> 01:14:50,522
- [Crow] Ken is sick.

2021
01:14:50,522 --> 01:14:52,514
Just ask Barbie.

2022
01:14:52,514 --> 01:14:53,800
- If we can get out of these bonds,

2023
01:14:53,800 --> 01:14:55,537
he'll of missed his chance.

2024
01:14:55,537 --> 01:14:57,377
- [Joel] Buy bonds where you work a bank.

2025
01:14:57,377 --> 01:14:59,855
- [Tom] Well, alley-oop.

2026
01:14:59,855 --> 01:15:01,881
In the meantime there's
some exercises you can do

2027
01:15:01,881 --> 01:15:02,905
in your office or home.

2028
01:15:02,905 --> 01:15:04,665
And they're really good for your back.

2029
01:15:04,665 --> 01:15:06,570
- [Joel] Okay, one two three.

2030
01:15:06,570 --> 01:15:08,320
Now you try, come on.

2031
01:15:12,223 --> 01:15:15,079
- [Crow] Come on, lay back down.

2032
01:15:15,079 --> 01:15:16,579
- If I can stretch these
bonds I may be able

2033
01:15:16,579 --> 01:15:18,928
to slip them over my wrist.

2034
01:15:18,928 --> 01:15:23,011
- [Tom] Yes, if you see,
I can stretch the bonds.

2035
01:15:25,483 --> 01:15:26,483
Space Ghost!

2036
01:15:29,112 --> 01:15:32,811
- [Crow] I think they're losing altitude.

2037
01:15:32,811 --> 01:15:35,528
- [Tom] This is Walter
Cronkite with Roger Mudd,

2038
01:15:35,528 --> 01:15:38,070
and we're space pirates hoo-hoo-hoo-hooo.

2039
01:15:38,070 --> 01:15:40,576
- [Joel] That's the way it was.

2040
01:15:40,576 --> 01:15:42,742
- This is Casa 7 central station, come in.

2041
01:15:42,742 --> 01:15:45,377
- Rinkman here, making
approach for landing.

2042
01:15:45,377 --> 01:15:48,281
- Neutralize all circuits, activate gyros.

2043
01:15:48,281 --> 01:15:49,114
- [Joel] And bring me one.

2044
01:15:49,114 --> 01:15:50,959
- We'll handle circuits and gyros.

2045
01:15:50,959 --> 01:15:54,597
- Ground control will bring
you in for landing, out.

2046
01:15:54,597 --> 01:15:56,507
- [Crow] Ah, let's see.

2047
01:15:56,507 --> 01:15:58,221
A couple of these, a couple of those.

2048
01:15:58,221 --> 01:15:59,537
Hit that one, there we go.

2049
01:15:59,537 --> 01:16:02,896
- [Joel] Ah, if it's not
one thing it's another.

2050
01:16:02,896 --> 01:16:03,813
Ah brother.

2051
01:16:05,110 --> 01:16:07,777
- [Tom] I saw the harbor lights.

2052
01:16:10,874 --> 01:16:11,952
- [Joel] Kids, check it out.

2053
01:16:11,952 --> 01:16:15,030
They're landing on the cover
of a popular science magazine.

2054
01:16:15,030 --> 01:16:16,113
- [Tom] Cool.

2055
01:16:23,206 --> 01:16:24,039
Kill the props.

2056
01:16:24,039 --> 01:16:25,087
- Well, we made it Doc.

2057
01:16:25,087 --> 01:16:27,344
- Now we have to take over Casa 7.

2058
01:16:27,344 --> 01:16:28,634
- And do it fast.

2059
01:16:28,634 --> 01:16:30,101
Get Markov and Link in here.

2060
01:16:30,101 --> 01:16:34,268
- [Tom] Oh, why don't you
take Linkov and Mark in there?

2061
01:16:35,373 --> 01:16:38,016
- [Crow] Avon calling?

2062
01:16:38,016 --> 01:16:42,127
- [Joel] Hi, I ran up here
all the way to meet you.

2063
01:16:42,127 --> 01:16:44,271
- [Tom] Gene Kelly! Look.

2064
01:16:44,271 --> 01:16:45,777
- First there's Paul
Ray, take him prisoner.

2065
01:16:45,777 --> 01:16:47,388
He's in charge of the
entire project of Casa 7.

2066
01:16:47,388 --> 01:16:48,221
- Then what?

2067
01:16:48,221 --> 01:16:49,437
- After that it will be easy.

2068
01:16:49,437 --> 01:16:50,824
- Where do we find this Paul Ray?

2069
01:16:50,824 --> 01:16:51,845
- I'll show you.

2070
01:16:51,845 --> 01:16:53,080
- [Crow] Here let me show you around.

2071
01:16:53,080 --> 01:16:56,332
We'll take over and
then we'll grab a beer.

2072
01:16:56,332 --> 01:16:58,234
- [Joel] Okay, now I want
you to do your space math.

2073
01:16:58,234 --> 01:17:01,338
Space two plus space
two equals space four.

2074
01:17:01,338 --> 01:17:02,921
- Rinkman.

2075
01:17:02,921 --> 01:17:04,876
- Just making a little surprise visit.

2076
01:17:04,876 --> 01:17:07,914
- [Tom] What are you doing
in Alan Brady's office?

2077
01:17:07,914 --> 01:17:08,844
- [Voiceover] We've covered the area

2078
01:17:08,844 --> 01:17:11,344
at least a dozen times, Winky.

2079
01:17:12,790 --> 01:17:13,655
- [Crow] Yeah! Get Winky.

2080
01:17:13,655 --> 01:17:15,517
Get him, get him, get Winky.

2081
01:17:15,517 --> 01:17:16,853
- [Joel] Yeah, hit him hard!

2082
01:17:16,853 --> 01:17:17,686
Really hard.

2083
01:17:17,686 --> 01:17:19,454
- [Tom] Are you guys hungry
for dinner I've got (muffled)

2084
01:17:19,454 --> 01:17:22,677
- [Joel] Hey, it's the
Nelsons, full and half.

2085
01:17:22,677 --> 01:17:24,486
- Hold it, or I'll use this.

2086
01:17:24,486 --> 01:17:25,319
- [Crow] Now do bobby!

2087
01:17:25,319 --> 01:17:26,736
- I said hold it!

2088
01:17:27,888 --> 01:17:29,058
- [Tom] Tickle me, (giggles)

2089
01:17:29,058 --> 01:17:31,366
- If you don't think so, I'll
give you a taste of this.

2090
01:17:31,366 --> 01:17:32,884
- [Joel] It's chocolate, hmm.

2091
01:17:32,884 --> 01:17:34,536
- I think it's slipping loose.

2092
01:17:34,536 --> 01:17:35,369
- [Crow] Yeah, right.

2093
01:17:35,369 --> 01:17:38,535
Would you like to hear my plan?

2094
01:17:38,535 --> 01:17:40,868
- [Tom] There, see? Told ya.

2095
01:17:42,020 --> 01:17:44,855
- [Joel] Ah, don't start
walking yet, Rocky.

2096
01:17:44,855 --> 01:17:46,069
- [Crow] No, it's time for a granola bar.

2097
01:17:46,069 --> 01:17:47,736
I need quick energy.

2098
01:17:51,226 --> 01:17:52,292
- [Tom] Ooh, my wrist.

2099
01:17:52,292 --> 01:17:54,938
- [Joel] Hey, why is that
ladder hanging sideways?

2100
01:17:54,938 --> 01:17:56,452
- [Tom] 'Cause it's space, get it?

2101
01:17:56,452 --> 01:17:57,702
See it's space.

2102
01:18:01,605 --> 01:18:03,730
- Ken keeps on the automatic lock.

2103
01:18:03,730 --> 01:18:06,479
- He didn't know there's
a way to handle that.

2104
01:18:06,479 --> 01:18:07,312
- [Crow] With a handle.

2105
01:18:07,312 --> 01:18:10,979
- There's an emergency
circuit breaker here.

2106
01:18:14,978 --> 01:18:17,268
- [Joel] It's the sign of pizza.

2107
01:18:17,268 --> 01:18:20,268
- [Crow] Whoa, watch that last step.

2108
01:18:21,108 --> 01:18:23,691
Oh no, the anarchists are here.

2109
01:18:27,588 --> 01:18:28,636
- [Joel] Good thing I happen to have

2110
01:18:28,636 --> 01:18:30,969
some sandpaper in my pocket.

2111
01:18:32,151 --> 01:18:35,734
- [Crow] Heh-heh-hey,
I always carry chalk.

2112
01:18:36,982 --> 01:18:38,573
- [Tom] Let's see.

2113
01:18:38,573 --> 01:18:39,906
Winky is a dolt.

2114
01:18:43,105 --> 01:18:45,016
- [Joel] Oh, that's in
breakfast of champions.

2115
01:18:45,016 --> 01:18:45,968
- [Crow] I remember.

2116
01:18:45,968 --> 01:18:47,885
- [Tom] Oh, I remember.

2117
01:18:52,988 --> 01:18:56,155
- [Tom] Whoa-ho, almost fooled myself.

2118
01:18:59,665 --> 01:19:01,998
- [Crow] It's cold filtered.

2119
01:19:03,396 --> 01:19:05,201
- [Tom] Hands off green man.

2120
01:19:05,201 --> 01:19:06,749
- The Orbit Jet is invisible.

2121
01:19:06,749 --> 01:19:09,003
I don't think Ken will
be able to find it again.

2122
01:19:09,003 --> 01:19:11,765
- I am frank to say, I am puzzled.

2123
01:19:11,765 --> 01:19:13,177
- [Joel] Well said, Martian

2124
01:19:13,177 --> 01:19:14,585
- Ken had the platform marked so he'd know

2125
01:19:14,585 --> 01:19:16,237
where the invisible ship was located.

2126
01:19:16,237 --> 01:19:18,605
I erased the marks and put
them on another platform.

2127
01:19:18,605 --> 01:19:22,689
- [Crow] Aren't I sneaky? (giggles)

2128
01:19:22,689 --> 01:19:24,825
- [Joel] Oh you kook, imagine his surprise

2129
01:19:24,825 --> 01:19:26,024
when his skull hits the pavement.

2130
01:19:26,024 --> 01:19:27,274
You're so nuts.

2131
01:19:29,040 --> 01:19:30,711
- The Orbit Jet's invisible.

2132
01:19:30,711 --> 01:19:31,840
I marked the platform.

2133
01:19:31,840 --> 01:19:32,739
Come on.

2134
01:19:32,739 --> 01:19:34,314
- [Tom] Now, let's tune into Ken's face

2135
01:19:34,314 --> 01:19:37,147
as he tries to find the Orbit Jet.

2136
01:19:39,049 --> 01:19:40,483
- We'll walk right into
the invisible band.

2137
01:19:40,483 --> 01:19:42,979
- [Tom] And watch my
face here when I try to--

2138
01:19:42,979 --> 01:19:44,359
- Where is this invisible band?

2139
01:19:44,359 --> 01:19:45,975
- I don't understand it.

2140
01:19:45,975 --> 01:19:47,444
- You sure you know what you're doing?

2141
01:19:47,444 --> 01:19:48,801
- I left the ship right here twice--

2142
01:19:48,801 --> 01:19:51,734
- [Crow] Maybe an invisible
tow truck came and, no.

2143
01:19:51,734 --> 01:19:53,537
- There's nothing here, real or invisible.

2144
01:19:53,537 --> 01:19:55,735
- Rocky Jones and the Martian
are on the ship, tied up.

2145
01:19:55,735 --> 01:19:56,932
- [Tom] I said it, and I'm glad.

2146
01:19:56,932 --> 01:19:59,544
- If I know Rocky Jones, he
didn't stay tied up long.

2147
01:19:59,544 --> 01:20:00,580
- But he couldn't get away.

2148
01:20:00,580 --> 01:20:02,718
- If he did, he's got the Orbit Jet.

2149
01:20:02,718 --> 01:20:04,610
And Cleolatra will have your neck.

2150
01:20:04,610 --> 01:20:05,858
- I'll find the ship.

2151
01:20:05,858 --> 01:20:08,953
- [Joel] If I have to
search all three pads.

2152
01:20:08,953 --> 01:20:10,472
- I'll get Rocky's crew into my ship

2153
01:20:10,472 --> 01:20:12,309
and send them along to Ophicius.

2154
01:20:12,309 --> 01:20:13,356
- With his friends in danger,

2155
01:20:13,356 --> 01:20:16,126
Rocky Jones will soon show his hand.

2156
01:20:16,126 --> 01:20:18,669
- Yes, you took the words
right out of my mind, Doc.

2157
01:20:18,669 --> 01:20:20,488
- [Tom] What do you do, old man?

2158
01:20:20,488 --> 01:20:22,758
- If the Orbit Jet is lost, so are you.

2159
01:20:22,758 --> 01:20:24,773
- [Crow] Oh I'm sorry your majesty.

2160
01:20:24,773 --> 01:20:28,026
Oh where did the rocket,
oh ho, no stepping.

2161
01:20:28,026 --> 01:20:30,526
- [Joel] An American in Paris.

2162
01:20:35,683 --> 01:20:36,881
- Were you looking for me, Ken?

2163
01:20:36,881 --> 01:20:38,728
- [Crow] No, I was looking for...

2164
01:20:38,728 --> 01:20:39,645
This chair!

2165
01:20:40,716 --> 01:20:41,716
That was it!

2166
01:20:43,295 --> 01:20:47,256
- [Joel] Oh, I can't
believe I fell for that.

2167
01:20:47,256 --> 01:20:48,562
- [Tom] Look, just answer my question.

2168
01:20:48,562 --> 01:20:50,562
Who are you looking for?

2169
01:20:54,372 --> 01:20:56,342
- Alright, I've got a nice place for you.

2170
01:20:56,342 --> 01:20:59,667
- [Joel] It's a Days Inn, it's
not elaborate but it's clean.

2171
01:20:59,667 --> 01:21:00,500
- Move.

2172
01:21:00,500 --> 01:21:05,076
- [Crow] Haha, I'm a grim old
warrior. Ho ho ho (whimpers)

2173
01:21:05,076 --> 01:21:07,338
- [Tom] Okay okay, that's perfect Steve.

2174
01:21:07,338 --> 01:21:09,751
Yeah, good special effect,
really tricks the eye.

2175
01:21:09,751 --> 01:21:11,751
- [Joel] It's Edith Ann.

2176
01:21:15,431 --> 01:21:19,550
- [Crow] Just a little
paint, cover the rust.

2177
01:21:19,550 --> 01:21:22,133
- [Tom] What? Silly putty, why?

2178
01:21:27,701 --> 01:21:29,891
- [Crow] Oh man, he's whiping
boogers on the rocket.

2179
01:21:29,891 --> 01:21:32,441
- [Tom] Those some big
boogers, let me tell ya.

2180
01:21:32,441 --> 01:21:37,216
- [Joel] Now I've gotta go
change the sand in the ashtrays.

2181
01:21:37,216 --> 01:21:38,609
- [Crow] Funny how things change, huh?

2182
01:21:38,609 --> 01:21:41,942
Funny how the hunter becomes the hunted.

2183
01:21:44,594 --> 01:21:46,617
- Who's ship is that on the next platform?

2184
01:21:46,617 --> 01:21:48,897
- [Tom] Oh, that's the
good ship, Lollipop.

2185
01:21:48,897 --> 01:21:50,411
- Who's ship is it?

2186
01:21:50,411 --> 01:21:52,444
- [Joel] Go ahead on three!

2187
01:21:52,444 --> 01:21:54,737
- Sounds like Kens in trouble.

2188
01:21:54,737 --> 01:21:55,987
Hold them here.

2189
01:21:59,974 --> 01:22:00,807
- Go on.

2190
01:22:02,801 --> 01:22:04,877
- [Crow] That's so cool, it's
like Romulan cloaking device.

2191
01:22:04,877 --> 01:22:06,218
The Klingon's had one too.

2192
01:22:06,218 --> 01:22:09,126
- [Tom] Oh jeeze, I really had to go.

2193
01:22:09,126 --> 01:22:11,293
I feel ten pounds lighter.

2194
01:22:14,050 --> 01:22:15,656
- [Joel] Now let's see, is that not it?

2195
01:22:15,656 --> 01:22:16,490
Or is it down there not it.

2196
01:22:16,490 --> 01:22:18,582
- [Crow] Your pockets are speaking to you,

2197
01:22:18,582 --> 01:22:19,614
they're trying to tell you something.

2198
01:22:19,614 --> 01:22:21,234
- [Tom] Ooo, kill. Kill.

2199
01:22:21,234 --> 01:22:23,662
- [Joel] Wait a minute,
I'm a young Buddy Ebsen.

2200
01:22:23,662 --> 01:22:26,128
- [Crow] That's impossible.

2201
01:22:26,128 --> 01:22:27,838
- Nobody's in sight.

2202
01:22:27,838 --> 01:22:29,136
Lock them in the rear section.

2203
01:22:29,136 --> 01:22:30,405
They've got a long journey ahead.

2204
01:22:30,405 --> 01:22:31,580
- Right, lets go.

2205
01:22:31,580 --> 01:22:32,624
- Link.

2206
01:22:32,624 --> 01:22:35,621
- [Tom] (gasps) We can have
the interrogation outside!

2207
01:22:35,621 --> 01:22:37,307
- Doc will go along as navigator.

2208
01:22:37,307 --> 01:22:38,499
- When do we blast off?

2209
01:22:38,499 --> 01:22:40,340
- As soon as I contact
Cleolantra and explain

2210
01:22:40,340 --> 01:22:41,480
- [Crow] Cleo Laine?

2211
01:22:41,480 --> 01:22:42,961
- I'll give you the word.

2212
01:22:42,961 --> 01:22:45,256
Markov and I will be
using Paul Ray's quarters.

2213
01:22:45,256 --> 01:22:47,782
- [Joel] Gene, you keep
singing and dancing.

2214
01:22:47,782 --> 01:22:49,040
- [Tom] Gotta dance.

2215
01:22:49,040 --> 01:22:50,111
- [Crow] Make it tight.

2216
01:22:50,111 --> 01:22:51,871
No, tighter, I can get out of this.

2217
01:22:51,871 --> 01:22:52,704
Make it tighter.

2218
01:22:52,704 --> 01:22:54,197
- Ken won't give us any more trouble.

2219
01:22:54,197 --> 01:22:55,567
- [Tom] Oh thanks for the update, Quisp.

2220
01:22:55,567 --> 01:22:59,022
- He's wanted back on Earth
to answer for his crimes.

2221
01:22:59,022 --> 01:23:01,785
- Perhaps he'll answer
for them sooner than that.

2222
01:23:01,785 --> 01:23:03,017
- What do you mean Hagar Nu?

2223
01:23:03,017 --> 01:23:05,597
- I wanted to be certain
that traitors are destroyed.

2224
01:23:05,597 --> 01:23:08,598
I inserted Toenite-Alpha
into the rocket tubes

2225
01:23:08,598 --> 01:23:10,241
of Rickman's spaceship.

2226
01:23:10,241 --> 01:23:12,266
- That'll blow them to
bits when they blast off.

2227
01:23:12,266 --> 01:23:13,273
- Yes.

2228
01:23:13,273 --> 01:23:14,866
The traitors will be destroyed.

2229
01:23:14,866 --> 01:23:18,132
- [Joel] And it will leave a huge stain.

2230
01:23:18,132 --> 01:23:21,132
- [Tom] I don't get ze Earth people.

2231
01:23:25,485 --> 01:23:27,054
- Winky, Paul?

2232
01:23:27,054 --> 01:23:27,887
- [Joel] Scooter.

2233
01:23:27,887 --> 01:23:28,720
- [Crow] Diane.

2234
01:23:28,720 --> 01:23:29,553
- [Tom] Chopper.

2235
01:23:29,553 --> 01:23:30,386
- [Joel] Chief.

2236
01:23:30,386 --> 01:23:31,219
- [Crow] McCloud.

2237
01:23:31,219 --> 01:23:32,052
Rawr.

2238
01:23:36,212 --> 01:23:39,295
- [Joel] Oh, now it's a Phaedo farce.

2239
01:23:40,824 --> 01:23:44,153
- Doctor Vanko, Link, come in.

2240
01:23:44,153 --> 01:23:45,563
- [Crow] I'll get it.

2241
01:23:45,563 --> 01:23:46,627
- Yeah, Rinkman?

2242
01:23:46,627 --> 01:23:48,558
- You can blast off anytime, Doc.

2243
01:23:48,558 --> 01:23:51,325
- What did you arrange with Cleolantra?

2244
01:23:51,325 --> 01:23:53,440
- She sending two spaceships with troops

2245
01:23:53,440 --> 01:23:55,040
to police this project.

2246
01:23:55,040 --> 01:23:57,249
- Can you hold on 'till they arrive?

2247
01:23:57,249 --> 01:23:58,972
- The troops will be taking over

2248
01:23:58,972 --> 01:24:01,677
before the people here
know Paul Ray's missing.

2249
01:24:01,677 --> 01:24:03,321
Come back as soon as you can, Doc.

2250
01:24:03,321 --> 01:24:04,975
- [Tom] I miss you, miss you a lot.

2251
01:24:04,975 --> 01:24:07,441
- And for you, good hunting.

2252
01:24:07,441 --> 01:24:09,137
You'll have to find Rocky Jones.

2253
01:24:09,137 --> 01:24:11,146
- [Joel] Good fishing,
good camping, good eating.

2254
01:24:11,146 --> 01:24:12,525
- Rinkman.

2255
01:24:12,525 --> 01:24:14,942
- [Crow] I found Rocky Jones!

2256
01:24:16,304 --> 01:24:17,929
- Where are Paul Ray and my crew?

2257
01:24:17,929 --> 01:24:19,395
- [Rinkman] You're a little late, Rocky.

2258
01:24:19,395 --> 01:24:20,228
- Where are they?

2259
01:24:20,228 --> 01:24:22,280
- [Rinkman] They're
due to blast off Casa 7

2260
01:24:22,280 --> 01:24:23,113
at any moment.

2261
01:24:23,113 --> 01:24:24,521
- On which ship?

2262
01:24:24,521 --> 01:24:26,598
- [Tom] There's only two ships out there!

2263
01:24:26,598 --> 01:24:27,646
- On my spaceship.

2264
01:24:27,646 --> 01:24:29,550
- Don't let them blast off, Rinkman.

2265
01:24:29,550 --> 01:24:30,766
- Stop bluffing, Rocky.

2266
01:24:30,766 --> 01:24:32,369
You try to hold the ship.

2267
01:24:32,369 --> 01:24:35,145
- You've gotta stop them, the
ships in danger of blowing up.

2268
01:24:35,145 --> 01:24:37,519
- [Tom] Folks, lets relive
the scene we just did.

2269
01:24:37,519 --> 01:24:38,936
Only this time...

2270
01:24:41,928 --> 01:24:43,968
- [Crow] Whoa, shook myself up.

2271
01:24:43,968 --> 01:24:46,421
Never really did that before.

2272
01:24:46,421 --> 01:24:47,809
- [Joel] Will the person
with the shiny rocket

2273
01:24:47,809 --> 01:24:48,642
please move it?

2274
01:24:48,642 --> 01:24:49,725
It's glaring.

2275
01:24:51,149 --> 01:24:52,345
- Starboard rocket.

2276
01:24:52,345 --> 01:24:54,374
- [Crow] I'm wearing my
strip of bacon today.

2277
01:24:54,374 --> 01:24:56,624
(coughing)

2278
01:24:59,122 --> 01:25:02,006
- [Joel] Ah, somebody jammed
a potato in the exhaust pipe.

2279
01:25:02,006 --> 01:25:03,535
- Ja, it registers.

2280
01:25:03,535 --> 01:25:06,366
- Try the starboard rocket again.

2281
01:25:06,366 --> 01:25:08,501
- [Crow] Jeeze, I was
just talking to my analyst

2282
01:25:08,501 --> 01:25:11,028
and things got weird.

2283
01:25:11,028 --> 01:25:13,696
- Dr. Vanko, Link, come in, urgent.

2284
01:25:13,696 --> 01:25:16,111
(buzzing)

2285
01:25:16,111 --> 01:25:17,924
- That's a signal, Doc, take it.

2286
01:25:17,924 --> 01:25:18,912
- [Tom] Yo.

2287
01:25:18,912 --> 01:25:19,814
- Dr. Vanko.

2288
01:25:19,814 --> 01:25:21,081
- Doc, trouble.

2289
01:25:21,081 --> 01:25:23,024
Rocky Jones' on his way to the ship.

2290
01:25:23,024 --> 01:25:24,402
Hold blastoff, take him.

2291
01:25:24,402 --> 01:25:26,244
- We'll handle him.

2292
01:25:26,244 --> 01:25:27,981
- [Joel] Yes, it's Dr.
Smith and Mr. Mooney

2293
01:25:27,981 --> 01:25:30,609
as you've never seen them before.

2294
01:25:30,609 --> 01:25:32,022
- [Crow] Romeo, Romeo, where..

2295
01:25:32,022 --> 01:25:35,272
- Open the hatch, then keep me covered.

2296
01:25:38,542 --> 01:25:40,143
- [Tom] Okay, now, turn off the lights

2297
01:25:40,143 --> 01:25:44,310
and when he comes in, oh
this is gonna be so good.

2298
01:25:46,957 --> 01:25:48,948
- [All Three] (doing Ancient
Battle theme from Star Trek)

2299
01:25:48,948 --> 01:25:50,698
- [Tom] Oh forget it.

2300
01:25:53,887 --> 01:25:54,821
- [Joel] I have this.

2301
01:25:54,821 --> 01:25:56,593
- Take Vanko, this ones mine.

2302
01:25:56,593 --> 01:25:58,065
- [Crow] And away!

2303
01:25:58,065 --> 01:26:00,148
- [Joel] Good job, Winky.

2304
01:26:04,168 --> 01:26:07,052
- [Tom] Ooh, right in the winky, ow.

2305
01:26:07,052 --> 01:26:10,469
- [Joel] That's for Betty, and for Tawny.

2306
01:26:13,962 --> 01:26:16,129
- [Tom] Whoa, whoa, Winky!

2307
01:26:18,288 --> 01:26:21,455
- [Joel] Oh, just in time square-butt.

2308
01:26:23,606 --> 01:26:25,969
- I knew Rocky was alright, Vena.

2309
01:26:25,969 --> 01:26:27,049
- [Tom] You don't know
nothing, you little punk.

2310
01:26:27,049 --> 01:26:28,129
- Of course, Bobby.

2311
01:26:28,129 --> 01:26:31,315
- Oh Paul, you don't know how
close you came to oblivion.

2312
01:26:31,315 --> 01:26:34,446
Hagar Nu loaded the
rockets with Toenite-Alpha.

2313
01:26:34,446 --> 01:26:35,467
- Wow.

2314
01:26:35,467 --> 01:26:37,098
It was lucky I thought of knocking out

2315
01:26:37,098 --> 01:26:38,567
those fuel pumps, wasn't it?

2316
01:26:38,567 --> 01:26:40,457
- I knew we could depend on you, Winky.

2317
01:26:40,457 --> 01:26:42,588
- Bobby showed us a new
trick with his pen knife.

2318
01:26:42,588 --> 01:26:44,990
- [Tom] It's a tracheotomy.

2319
01:26:44,990 --> 01:26:47,509
- I had to do something, didn't I, Rocky?

2320
01:26:47,509 --> 01:26:49,124
Well that's why you took me along.

2321
01:26:49,124 --> 01:26:51,555
- Bobby, you're wonderful.

2322
01:26:51,555 --> 01:26:53,725
Oh Paul, there are a couple more prisoners

2323
01:26:53,725 --> 01:26:56,009
at your quarters we have
to pick up to add to these.

2324
01:26:56,009 --> 01:26:57,350
- [Joel] And throw Bobby in there.

2325
01:26:57,350 --> 01:26:59,426
- Oh, did you find the Orbit Jet?

2326
01:26:59,426 --> 01:27:01,102
- Yes, and she's ready for blastoff.

2327
01:27:01,102 --> 01:27:02,089
- [Tom] And so am I.

2328
01:27:02,089 --> 01:27:03,412
- Paul, one more detail.

2329
01:27:03,412 --> 01:27:04,245
- [Crow] Bite me.

2330
01:27:04,245 --> 01:27:05,751
- There are two spaceships
headed here from Ophicius.

2331
01:27:05,751 --> 01:27:09,418
- I'll know what to do
with them, blast 'em.

2332
01:27:11,434 --> 01:27:13,899
- [Joel] Oh, happiness fades
back to the dark recesses

2333
01:27:13,899 --> 01:27:15,482
of my hideous life.

2334
01:27:17,103 --> 01:27:18,314
- [All Three] Yoroniku, Gamera.

2335
01:27:18,314 --> 01:27:21,481
Yoroniku, Gamera. Yoroniku, Ga-mer-ah!

2336
01:27:24,789 --> 01:27:26,597
- [Crow] Looks like you
got the worst of it, Ned.

2337
01:27:26,597 --> 01:27:27,665
- Hey, Rocky.

2338
01:27:27,665 --> 01:27:30,418
What time do we land on Earth
with our cargo of traitors?

2339
01:27:30,418 --> 01:27:32,277
- [Joel] Yeah, why, is
Betty waiting for you?

2340
01:27:32,277 --> 01:27:33,527
- Oh wonderful.

2341
01:27:34,409 --> 01:27:36,146
Hey, how about using the astrophone?

2342
01:27:36,146 --> 01:27:37,731
- I've already reported to Secretary--

2343
01:27:37,731 --> 01:27:39,510
- [Tom] Nah nah nah,
not tonight plant Winky.

2344
01:27:39,510 --> 01:27:42,171
- Yeah, well, uh, you see,
I wanted to call Betty.

2345
01:27:42,171 --> 01:27:43,969
I wanna see if she's till waiting for me

2346
01:27:43,969 --> 01:27:45,501
at the bandstand in Central Park.

2347
01:27:45,501 --> 01:27:47,875
- [Crow] Do it! Space whack him dead!

2348
01:27:47,875 --> 01:27:49,499
- I'll ask her if she
has a friend for you.

2349
01:27:49,499 --> 01:27:51,749
(laughter)

2350
01:27:52,920 --> 01:27:54,003
- [Tom] Is this it, is this it?

2351
01:27:54,003 --> 01:27:54,896
I'm holding my breath.

2352
01:27:54,896 --> 01:27:55,931
Is this it?

2353
01:27:55,931 --> 01:27:58,181
(cheering)

2354
01:28:13,627 --> 01:28:14,640
- Hello Earth!

2355
01:28:14,640 --> 01:28:15,473
- Bzzz.

2356
01:28:16,863 --> 01:28:18,119
No, you see, Joel, the
thing is that I can't--

2357
01:28:18,119 --> 01:28:18,952
Bzzzzz.

2358
01:28:20,279 --> 01:28:21,954
Now how would you like it
if someone came up and--

2359
01:28:21,954 --> 01:28:25,704
Bzzz (imitating guitar solo)

2360
01:28:30,104 --> 01:28:31,211
Now, Joel, come on.

2361
01:28:31,211 --> 01:28:33,229
Being an amplifier
makes my innards vibrate

2362
01:28:33,229 --> 01:28:35,242
and that just makes me feel all funny.

2363
01:28:35,242 --> 01:28:36,297
- Oh, come on, Tom.

2364
01:28:36,297 --> 01:28:38,058
Crow's having a good time, aren't you?

2365
01:28:38,058 --> 01:28:39,341
- I wouldn't go that far, Joel.

2366
01:28:39,341 --> 01:28:41,504
And watch out for my
eyes, they're brand new.

2367
01:28:41,504 --> 01:28:42,979
- Here you guys, I'll sing a song.

2368
01:28:42,979 --> 01:28:44,697
That'll probably make you feel better.

2369
01:28:44,697 --> 01:28:46,799
Shadow me, okay, Mr. Amplifier?

2370
01:28:46,799 --> 01:28:50,216
- (imitates guitar riff)

2371
01:28:52,304 --> 01:28:54,470
♫ Sleepy little fella

2372
01:28:54,470 --> 01:28:57,096
♫ Nodding in my arms

2373
01:28:57,096 --> 01:29:01,009
♫ Couldn't keep your head up if you tried

2374
01:29:01,009 --> 01:29:02,010
- Oh I feel so much better now.

2375
01:29:02,010 --> 01:29:04,564
♫ Take a ship of slumber

2376
01:29:04,564 --> 01:29:07,499
♫ When nothing harms

2377
01:29:07,499 --> 01:29:12,148
♫ An astro-boy who's
on a star field ride ♫

2378
01:29:12,148 --> 01:29:15,709
- Joel, for God's sake,
I'm not a Stratocaster.

2379
01:29:15,709 --> 01:29:19,209
- (imitating guitar solo)

2380
01:29:24,566 --> 01:29:25,507
- Oh, I'm sorry you guys.

2381
01:29:25,507 --> 01:29:26,893
Listen, I got a, uh,

2382
01:29:26,893 --> 01:29:29,629
I got a letter here and put that up

2383
01:29:29,629 --> 01:29:31,111
stills there, Cambot.

2384
01:29:31,111 --> 01:29:33,898
This is from Tye Rickman, and
he's got some pictures there.

2385
01:29:33,898 --> 01:29:35,715
Cool, they're pretty neat aren't they?

2386
01:29:35,715 --> 01:29:36,548
- Hey, could you hurry it up?

2387
01:29:36,548 --> 01:29:38,333
I'm not sure how long I
can hold this position.

2388
01:29:38,333 --> 01:29:39,166
- Okay.

2389
01:29:39,166 --> 01:29:40,880
Alright, I'm gonna read Tye's letter

2390
01:29:40,880 --> 01:29:44,518
by using the golden
throat, okay, here we go.

2391
01:29:44,518 --> 01:29:45,675
- Oh no, Joel, not the golden throat.

2392
01:29:45,675 --> 01:29:50,260
♫ Wah-wow-wa-wow, I really love you

2393
01:29:50,260 --> 01:29:52,758
♫ I really dig your way hip show

2394
01:29:52,758 --> 01:29:54,733
♫ I tape you on Friday nights

2395
01:29:54,733 --> 01:29:58,071
♫ Watch you as you happen on Sat. Morning

2396
01:29:58,071 --> 01:30:01,067
♫ And watch the one I taped afterwards

2397
01:30:01,067 --> 01:30:05,234
♫ Back to back, it's the only way to go

2398
01:30:06,555 --> 01:30:09,035
♫ Tom Servo really need a woman

2399
01:30:09,035 --> 01:30:10,998
♫ Keep up the good work

2400
01:30:10,998 --> 01:30:11,980
♫ I really want ♫

2401
01:30:11,980 --> 01:30:13,306
Now now, come on, Joel.

2402
01:30:13,306 --> 01:30:15,179
On top of everything, I've got to put up

2403
01:30:15,179 --> 01:30:16,546
with these gratuitous insults.

2404
01:30:16,546 --> 01:30:19,097
And to think of all I do
for the ship around here.

2405
01:30:19,097 --> 01:30:20,774
Well I've simply had it, my friend.

2406
01:30:20,774 --> 01:30:21,637
- Hey, you know what?

2407
01:30:21,637 --> 01:30:23,311
Let's see what this system can really do.

2408
01:30:23,311 --> 01:30:25,940
Okay, here comes the beatdowns
and a windmill, here we go!

2409
01:30:25,940 --> 01:30:29,357
(gibberish guitar noise)

2410
01:30:32,967 --> 01:30:35,734
- What do you think, sirs?

2411
01:30:35,734 --> 01:30:38,757
- So any way, reading John-Paul Sartre

2412
01:30:38,757 --> 01:30:40,842
opened up a whole new world for me.

2413
01:30:40,842 --> 01:30:43,306
Suddenly, being a shift
supervisor at Arby's

2414
01:30:43,306 --> 01:30:44,970
wasn't enough anymore.

2415
01:30:44,970 --> 01:30:49,127
I had to say to myself, I have
to do what's right for Frank.

2416
01:30:49,127 --> 01:30:51,176
I have to do what's gonna make Frank

2417
01:30:51,176 --> 01:30:54,246
feel good in this cold
heartless modern world.

2418
01:30:54,246 --> 01:30:55,265
- Frank, when I get out of this,

2419
01:30:55,265 --> 01:30:56,581
I'm going to kill you.

2420
01:30:56,581 --> 01:30:59,360
- Ah, the existence of vague threats

2421
01:30:59,360 --> 01:31:01,127
that no one can do anything about.

2422
01:31:01,127 --> 01:31:02,505
- It's not a vague threat, Frank.

2423
01:31:02,505 --> 01:31:04,338
I'm going to kill you.

